{
  "rules": [
    "Model exhibits a strong upward drift bias when recent history shows volatility followed by a spike; true outcomes often reverse direction immediately after the model's peak.",
    "When sentiment shifts from positive (1.0) to negative (-1.0), the model fails to capture the subsequent mean reversion and continues forecasting higher prices.",
    "The model underestimates the magnitude of volatility spikes in the first 5-7 days, predicting smoother paths than the actual sharp increases seen in true outcomes.",
    "After a significant price spike (e.g., >70 EUR), the model's forecast trajectory becomes overly optimistic compared to the true outcome which frequently drops back below the pre-spike average within 10 days.",
    "Sentiment history lags behind price action; relying solely on sentiment leads to overconfidence in upward trends when recent volatility contradicts the current sentiment score."
  ]
}
